    "id" : 3,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 97.439, 541.767, 512.738, 587.422 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Proof. Since N is ﬁnitely generated, it follows from [13, Theorem 6.4] that there exists a chain 0 = N0 ⊂ N1 ⊂ ··· ⊂ Nk = N of submodules of N such that for each i we have Nj/Nj−1 ∼= R/pj with pj ∈ SuppN."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 4,
    "level" : "2",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 97.44, 521.448, 512.923, 546.862 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "(1) Note that HomR(R/I,E) is an injective R/I-module for any injective R-module E by [12, Lemma 3.5]. For each pj, by [15, Theorem 10.64], there is a spectral sequence"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 5,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 171.96, 490.167, 438.142, 511.897 ],
    "font" : "CMMI10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "E2p,q = ExtpR/I(R/pj,ExtqR(R/I,M)) ⇒ ExtnR(R/pj,M)."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 6,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 97.44, 409.287, 512.913, 485.257 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Being a subquotient of a ﬁnite direct sum of copies of ExtqR(R/I,M) ∈ S , we have that E2p,q ∈ S for 0 q n and any p. Since E∞p,q is isomorphic to a subquotient of E2p,q, we have E∞p,q ∈ S for 0 q n and any p. Hence ExtiR(R/pj,M) ∈ S for 0 i n. Consequently, applying the functor ExtiR(−,M) to exact sequences 0 → Nj−1 → Nj → Ni/Nj−1 → 0 yields that ExtiR(N,M) ∈ S for 0 i n."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 7,
    "level" : "2",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 114.361, 403.472, 387.983, 414.382 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "(2) can be proved similarly by using [15, Theorem 10.60]."
